Defend Your Experience
#60DaysOfClaudeAI — Day 50/60
An AI cross-examiner that reads your resume, LinkedIn bio, project write-up, research summary, or performance review — extracts every claim you make about yourself — and interviews you until your answers hold up in the real room.
This isn't a resume reviewer. It doesn't polish your bullet points. It questions them, the way a skeptical interviewer, investor, or panel would — and helps you build the evidence and confidence to defend what you claim.
How it works
1. Upload — Drop a .txt/.md/.csv file or paste your resume, bio, or write-up directly.
2. Set the context — Pick why you're preparing (job interview, performance review, funding pitch, academic defense, client pitch) and who's in the room (technical experts, HR, executives, mixed panel).
3. Case file — The app extracts 5–8 real claims from your material, ranks them by risk (vague/unquantified claims surface first), and stages them as "exhibits."
4. Cross-examination — One question at a time, in a live deposition-style transcript. Every answer shapes the next question — vague answers get pushed harder, strong answers get closed out and stamped Weak / Solid / Iron-clad.
5. Defense report — An overall defense score, a claim-by-claim confidence breakdown, and specific notes on what held up and what still needs sharpening — exportable as a text file.
Session history is saved locally so you can revisit past cases.
Tech stack
Single self-contained HTML file — zero external dependencies, fully offline UI
Vanilla JavaScript (no frameworks, no build step)
Claude (Sonnet) via the Anthropic Messages API for claim extraction and adaptive questioning
localStorage for session persistence
Hand-built SVG charts for score visualization — no charting libraries
Note on running it
The live interview (claim extraction, cross-examination, evaluation) calls the Anthropic API directly from the page and only works inside Claude's artifact preview, where authentication is handled automatically. Opening the downloaded HTML file in a plain browser will render the full interface, but API-dependent steps won't respond.
Why I built this
Fifty days into this challenge, most of what I've built has been about presenting experience — resumes, pitches, profiles. This one flips that: it assumes the presenting is done, and prepares you for the part that actually decides outcomes — being questioned on it, live, with no time to edit your answer.
